  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[fingerprint]` meets the built-in's criteria.\n\n- **Placement:** It sits on an explicit function with a body, so it can excuse that function's zero execution.\n- **Form:** The explanation is in fenced `{cite}` commentary, which the built-in accepts.\n- **Substance:** The reason is not just difficulty. `UnreadContents` is declared as `enum UnreadContents {}`, which has no variants. No value of it can exist, so `fingerprint(&self)` can never be called. The body `match *self {}` is an empty match with no executable case. The commentary says the impl exists only to satisfy the `Domain` associated-type bound. This agrees with `type NodeContent = UnreadContents` in `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]`.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The claim that the fixture cannot construct a value agrees with the enum declaration. The related `fn[node_content]` panics instead of returning a value, which supports it.\n- **Redundancy:** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same target, so the citation is not redundant.",
